Time Complexity:-

Time Complexity is a concept in computer science, that quantifies the amount of time an algorithm takes
to run as a function of length of its input.

It provides an estimate of the number of the basic operations (such as comparisons, assignments,
arithmetic operations, etc.) performed by the algorithm in relation to the size of the input data.

timecomplexity = f(length of input).
       y       = f(       x       ).

Worst time complexity = Big 'O' notation. f --> O
tc = O(length of input)

For Linear Search -- :
tc = O(N), where N = length of array/ no. of iterations across the array.

For Binary Search -- :
tc = O(logN), where N = length of array/ no. of iterations across the array.

List:

O(1) = Constant tc.
O(N) = Linear tc. -- ex) only one loop.
O(N^2) = Quadratic tc. -- ex) nested loops.
O(logN) = Logarithmic tc. -- ex) Binary Search.
O(10^N) = Exponential tc.
O(N!) = Factorial tc.